{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>הלא</b> — Another pericope, to mention the sin that they were divorcing their wives, who were weeping, on account of foreign women, as written in the book of Ezra. And it was incumbent upon them to take to heart, saying: Is not one father, Jacob, [ours]? If so, our father is one and our creator is one. Why do we deal treacherously, a man with his brother or with his sister? For on account of this pericope [they violate and] profane the covenant of our fathers who received the Torah."], :book :malachi, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The syntax of the final clause is strained; translated hyper-literally. It is unclear whether לחלל is transitive (they profane the covenant) or whether the subject shifts mid-clause."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Malachi -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/malachi"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:14.019209932Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}